  "query_preview": "..\nA dryer pattern begins to move into the Marianas as the last of the\nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms associated with Jangmi\nhave shifted west of the region. The Marianas will be mostly dry\ntonight before a weak trade wind trough moves through, bumping up\nshower coverage from isolated to scattered Saturday. Moisture will\nremain high enough to retain at least isolated showers for the rest\nof the forecast period. The potential for lighter winds by mid next \nweek may allow for some island effect showers to develop but this\nremains uncertain.",
